# Apixaban + 10 CHCl3: cheap XTB2 pre-equilibration MD, WITH spherical confinement
# Analogous to the Water/DMSO/MeOH confined XTB2 pre-equilibration runs
# (Apixaban/Water/MD/Apixaban_10H2O_XTB_preequil_confined.inp,
#  Apixaban/DMSO/MD/10/Apixaban_10DMSO_XTB_preequil_confined.inp,
#  Apixaban/MeOH/MD/10/Apixaban_10MeOH_XTB_preequil_confined.inp).
#
# UPDATED: now uses the real chloroform-optimized Apixaban geometry
#   (Apixaban_SMD_chloroform_Opt_Freq_KeepDens.xyz, r2SCAN-3c/SMD(chloroform),
#   converged, no imaginary frequency) instead of the earlier placeholder
#   (DMSO-optimized geometry). The Apixaban centroid came out essentially
#   identical to the other solvents' (31.537, -19.865, -0.109), so the
#   confinement sphere parameters are unchanged.
#
# Starting geometry: Apixaban_SMD_chloroform_Opt_Freq_KeepDens.xyz + 10 CHCl3
#   monomers (idealized tetrahedral geometry, C-H=1.09 Ang, C-Cl=1.77 Ang),
#   each placed with its C atom on the same 12-direction, radius-12.78-Angstrom
#   sphere-shell pattern used for the original Explicit10 Water/DMSO/MeOH
#   placements (offsets reused verbatim). Orientation of each CHCl3 molecule
#   is arbitrary (not hand-rotated).
#   Built programmatically; min initial solvent-Apixaban distance = 2.45
#   Angstrom (no atom-overlapping clash).
#
# Cell Sphere: same confinement strategy as water/DMSO/MeOH - center =
#   Apixaban centroid of this structure (31.537, -19.865, -0.109), radius
#   14.0 Angstrom (Apixaban's own farthest atom from centroid is ~9.03 Ang),
#   spring constant 20 kJ/mol/Ang^2.
#
# Note: XTB2 is only used to generate a better-equilibrated starting geometry
#   for later r2SCAN-3c work - not for energetics used in the solvent
#   comparison.

! XTB2 MD

%md
  Timestep 1.0_fs
  Initvel 298.15_K
  Thermostat NHC 298.15_K Timecon 20.0_fs
  Cell Sphere 31.537, -19.865, -0.109, 14.0 Spring 20
  Dump Position Stride 100 Filename "Apixaban_10CHCl3_XTB_preequil_confined.xyz"
  Run 20000
end

